Map the BC texture formats to Metal pixel formats wherever the Metal backend
advertises TextureCompressionBC (PhysicalDeviceMTL.mm), not only on macOS.

On visionOS the feature is advertised when the GPU supports BC, but every BC
format fell into DAWN_UNREACHABLE(), aborting on the first BC texture (for
example a BC7 texture pack). Same fix rebelancap/dusklight-ios carries.

--- a/src/dawn/native/metal/UtilsMetal.mm	2026-09-30 19:38:21
+++ b/src/dawn/native/metal/UtilsMetal.mm	2026-09-30 19:38:21
@@ -405,7 +405,8 @@
             }
             return MTLPixelFormatStencil8;
 
-#if DAWN_PLATFORM_IS(MACOS)
+#if DAWN_PLATFORM_IS(MACOS) || \
+    (defined(__IPHONE_16_4) && __IPHONE_OS_VERSION_MIN_REQUIRED >= __IPHONE_16_4)
         case wgpu::TextureFormat::BC1RGBAUnorm:
             return MTLPixelFormatBC1_RGBA;
         case wgpu::TextureFormat::BC1RGBAUnormSrgb:
